    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd built-in support for [TeleOCR](https://github.com/caipeng328/TeleOCR), using the existing Qwen2.5-VL vision stack and a Qwen3 text decoder.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Register `TeleOCRForConditionalGeneration` without replacing the Qwen2.5-VL architecture globally.\n- Initialize Qwen3 with `hf_text_config`, including its head dimension and Q/K normalization, while retaining the existing multimodal processor and weight-loading path.\n- Add an example to the model initialization test registry and document the required architecture override. The official model-specific plugin is not needed.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll applicable staged-file pre-commit hooks passed during `git commit`, including mypy, Ruff, SPDX, Markdown, and test-tethering checks. `git diff --check 3fe917abb13160d60bea5330399f5c09ca282348 HEAD` passed. The squash retains the exact previously validated code tree.\n\nExternal integration used Ascend 910B, [vLLM 0.30.0](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607), [vllm-ascend](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/commit/16074608c71ef5adce4e2a4e475848b8fc037297), Torch 2.10.0, torch-npu 2.10.0.post4, Transformers 5.14.1, and CANN 9.1.0 B243. The model class was identical to this branch; the small base-class hook was equivalently ported to that runtime. This was **not** a full native current-main integration run, and no Ascend repository changes were required.\n\nCheckpoint: [`XingChen-AGI/TeleOCR`, revision `70a19ec6a3b036311af19ae5e762e650f41a5980`](https://huggingface.co/XingChen-AGI/TeleOCR/tree/70a19ec6a3b036311af19ae5e762e650f41a5980).\n\nActual serving command, with that checkpoint downloaded to `/task/models/TeleOCR`:\n\n```bash\nvllm serve /task/models/TeleOCR --host 127.0.0.1 --port 18193 \\\n  --served-model-name TeleOCR --trust-remote-code --enforce-eager \\\n  --max-model-len 4096 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.3 \\\n  --hf-overrides '{\"architectures\":[\"TeleOCRForConditionalGeneration\"]}'\n```\n\nExternal validation harness commands and results:\n\n| Command | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `python /task/probe_document.py` | Synthetic document OCR and layout checks passed; expected text and box/label structure were present. |\n| `python /task/load_http.py --kind document --requests 4 --concurrency 2 --output /task/results/load-document.json` | 4/4 requests succeeded. This is a bounded smoke check, not a throughput benchmark. |\n| `PYTHONPATH= /task/hf-reference-clean/bin/python /task/validate_reference.py` | Same-image, same-prompt greedy prefix matched the independent official HF model, CPU FP32 versus NPU BF16, up to 24 new tokens. Reference environment used Transformers 4.57.1. |\n\nThe harness scripts above are external to this PR. The registry addition is exercised by the existing `tests/models/test_initialization.py` Buildkite job; that full current-main test was not run locally. CUDA/ROCm, full OmniDocBench evaluation, and LoRA/TP/PP remain unverified. An additional all-files check was not clean: aggregate mypy failed, and the non-root wrapper test hit the macOS `/var` versus `/private/var` path mismatch. Changed-file checks passed; no claim of full-suite or CI success is made.\n\n## Details\n\nThe published checkpoint advertises Qwen2.5-VL, but its text decoder is Qwen3. Selecting the ordinary Qwen2 decoder therefore gives the wrong attention implementation. Passing the outer multimodal config to Qwen3 also fails because text attributes such as `vocab_size` are nested. A protected decoder-construction hook lets TeleOCR select Qwen3 with the text sub-configuration and reuse the vision implementation. The default Qwen2.5-VL construction is preserved.\n\nBefore submission, searches for TeleOCR, NaviDC, and NaviOCR found no existing matching PR. This adds a dedicated built-in architecture instead of the official external vLLM 0.11 plugin's global replacement. AI assistance was used to implement, validate, and prepare this contribution.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
